<title>CHINA: Cho Hung Bank sets US$100 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>Cho Hung Bank sets US$100 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by bookrunner BA Asia on Tuesday.</p>
<p>BORROWER  CHO HUNG BANK</p>
<p> AMOUNT    US$100 MLN  COUPON	6ML+40BP  MATURITY  1 YEAR</p>
<p> TYPE	FRN	   ISS PRICE   PAR	 LAUNCHED  14.JUL.97</p>
<p> PUTS	NONE	  CALLS	 NONE	PAY DATE  21.JUL.97</p>
<p> LISTING   LUXEMBOURG  REPAYMENT   BULLET    TAXATION  FREE&amp;CLR</p>
<p> RATING    BAA1 *	SALES LMTS  CUSTOMARY DENOMS    US$250K</p>
<p> NEG PLG   YES	   CRS DEF     YES	 FORCE MAJ IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW   U.S.	  HOME CTRY   S.KOREA   PAY FREQ SEMIANNUAL</p>
<p> FEES	12BP FLAT FOR MANAGEMENT AND UNDERWRITING</p>
<p> ARRANGER	BA ASIA (BOOKS)</p>
<p> PAY AGENT     CITIBANK, N.A.</p>
<p> NOTES	   *ISSUER RATING</p>
<p>		   DIRECT, UNSECURED, UNSUBORDINATED AND</p>
<p>		   UNCONDITIONAL DEBTS, RANKED PARI PASSU.</p>
<p>		   THE NOTES WILL BE ISSUED OFF THE BANK'S US$2.0</p>
<p>		   BLN GLOBAL MEDIUM-TERM NOTE PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>		   A GROUP IS BEING FORMED.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
